{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Et re'ehu.</b> [It means] 'with,' and likewise [in] the plural." "<b>Ve-nadchah.</b> From the nif'al binyan; and in the qal, 'the outcasts of Israel shall enter.'" "<b>Ba-garzen.</b> Iron with which one cuts wood, from the root [of] נגזרתי." "<b>Ve-nashal ha-barzel.</b> Like ונסע, from the root [of] כי תשל זיתך. Only here נשל is a transitive verb [פעל עומד], while נשלו גוים רבים is intransitive [יוצא]. Likewise קול גדול ולא יסף — according to one grammarian [it is one way], but in my opinion both [forms] are intransitive [יוצאים]."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {3 "Resolved 'על דעת מדקדק גדול' as 'according to one grammarian'; 'יוצא' and 'יוצאים' in Ibn Ezra's usage denote intransitive (lit. 'going out' of the subject). The categorical pairing of ולא יסף with the נשל discussion is obscure but translated faithfully."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:01.885672989Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}